{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ties.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":". Under that strict order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the minimum spanning forest is unique, and this is it, whichever algorithm runs: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"canonical forest, listed in nondecreasing weight and, among equal weights, in position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order, with the weight added up in that order. Currently Kruskal’s algorithm on sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) and otherwise Prim’s under that order followed by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sort of the n − 1 edges taken, which is faster on denser graphs (see the benchmarks).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop, never for a self-loop, and not kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Negative and zero weights are ordinary weights, and so are infinities. A NaN weight traps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(NetworkX instead offers ","type":"text"},{"code":"ignore_nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; filter such edges out first).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}]}],"name":"Complexity"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not overflow and is not NaN.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/Spannin